************STEPS TO PROCESS GPCP version 2.3 DATA********************

--2.5-degree longitude by 2.5-degree latitude
--Monthly resolution
--Units of average mm/month
--Adler, R.F., G.J. Huffman, A. Chang, R. Ferraro, P. Xie, 
  J. Janowiak, B. Rudolf, U. Schneider, S. Curtis, D. Bolvin,
  A. Gruber, J. Sussking, P. Arkin, 2003: The Version 2 Global 
  Precipitation Climatology Project (GPCP) Monthly Precipitation
  Analysis (1979-Present).  J. Hydrometeor., 4, 1147-1167.

1) Download the data from
   http://eagle1.umd.edu/GPCP_CDR/Monthly_Data/

   (Interim data can be found at:
    http://eagle1.umd.edu/GPCP_ICDR/GPCP_Monthly.html)

2) Convert the data from monthly means to monthly totals,
   and regrid to weather data resolution.
   --Use program gpcp_prep23.f90
   --Specify the years to convert
   --Check the units
      If using gpcp data for driver data comparison/calculations, 
           make sure flag_mmpmon=.false., which output units of mm/day.
      Otherwise, if flag_mmpmon=.true. then mm/month are output.

   --Compile (>make gpcp_prep23)
   --Run (>gpcp_prep23)

3) Check the global total precipitation
   --Use the program gpcp_checktot.f90
   --Provide the name of the file that you wish to check
   --Check the units (matching flag_mmpmon as in gpcp_prep23.f90)
   --Compile (>make gpcp_checktot)
   --Run (>gpcp_checktot)


